cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "analyticgrimu: Granularity testing for Mann-Whitney U-test reported results"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Forensic meta-science tools for checking whether reported Mann-Whitney U test
  results are mathematically possible. Published U statistics and p-values are
  rounded, so a reported value is consistent only if some attainable exact value
  falls within its rounding window. Given the two group sizes, the package
  enumerates every U statistic the test can produce and the p-values it implies
  under the reporting conventions of common software, then asks whether the
  reported statistic, p-value, and their pairing could have arisen together.
keywords:
  - meta-science
  - error detection
  - granularity testing
  - Mann-Whitney U
  - R
